{
  "$comment": "Maintainer-only manifest mapping each UPSTREAM-DERIVED bundled skill to its upstream source. Drives `pnpm skills:update` (scripts/sync-skills.ts), which resolves each repo@ref to a commit SHA (recorded in scripts/vendor/skills/skills-lock.json) and refreshes the raw-upstream cache under scripts/vendor/skills/ (SKILL.md plus `extraPaths`, relative to the upstream skill folder) so `git diff scripts/vendor/` shows what changed upstream since the last sync. The maintainer then hand-re-applies the de-JS / compat adaptation to the live bundled SKILL.md under src/integration/ai/skills/bundled/<name>/. Bundled skills are FROZEN committed source — this tooling never touches src/.",
  "$cleanRoom": [
    "ralphctl-karpathy-guidelines is clean-room (distilled from Andrej Karpathy's public X post https://x.com/karpathy/status/2015883857489522876 — concepts only, no upstream SKILL.md) — not sync-managed.",
    "ralphctl-ambition is clean-room (distilled from Felix Rieseberg's article https://felixrieseberg.com/how-to-be-more-ambitious-a-tutorial-for-humans-with-models/ — concepts only; robonuggets/be-ambitious is credited as prior art only, nothing copied) — not sync-managed.",
    "ralphctl-humanizer IS sync-managed below, but for drift review only: its pattern catalogue is paraphrased, never copied, because upstream derives it from Wikipedia's CC BY-SA \"Signs of AI writing\" page. Re-word any new upstream pattern in your own words. Bundled version tracks upstream 4.0.0 patterns (the vague \"the part\" stand-in under Staging, the \"Overall\"/\"Ultimately\" closer under Closers) in fresh wording. Upstream 4.0.0 step 2 (\"add a specific detail you know to be true\") was rejected: create-pr/template.md:18 forbids invention and the vendored 3.1.0 text (:15, :37) says to add nothing, so the bundled skill keeps \"Add nothing\". The stock-word list (pattern 10) and promotional examples (pattern 13) are rebuilt from upstream §12, §15 and §16 only."
  ],
